## WS-A: Security Hardening & Vulnerability Mitigation

### A1. CSRF Total Coverage Verification
- **Current state:** CSRF double-submit enforced on all `/api` POST/PUT/DELETE via `server/routes.ts:120`.
- **Gap:** WebSocket upgrade requests bypass CSRF. Verify that [wsCore.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/wsCore.ts) session validation is equivalent.
- **Action:** `ops/security/csrf-coverage-audit.ts` — Script that enumerates all Express routes from [server/routes.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes.ts) and flags any POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints not behind `enforceCsrf`.

### A2. End-to-End Encryption Audit
- **Current state:** At-rest AES-256-GCM in [crypto.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/crypto.ts), E2EE envelope in `e2ee.ts`.
- **Gap:** Export artifacts on MinIO are stored unencrypted. ClickHouse data-at-rest relies on disk-level only.
- **Action:** `ops/security/export-encryption-audit.ts` — Verify that [objectStorage.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/objectStorage.ts) passes server-side encryption headers (`x-amz-server-side-encryption`) to MinIO.
- **Headlamp Enhancement Recommendation:** Add a Headlamp plugin panel showing KES key rotation status and MinIO SSE-KMS configuration. Deploy via `ops/kubernetes/headlamp-kes-plugin.yaml`.

### A3. Secure Transport Verification
- **Current state:** TLS forced at ingress (`ssl-redirect: true`), `ENCRYPTION_KEY` validated at boot.
- **Gap:** Internal cluster traffic (API→ClickHouse, API→MinIO, API→Valkey) is plaintext.
- **Action:** Add to `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_INTERNAL_TLS.md` — Document how to enable Valkey TLS (`--tls-port`, `--tls-cert-file`), ClickHouse HTTPS interface, and MinIO `--certs-dir`. Track with `ops/alerts/internal-tls-alerts.yaml`.

### A4. Attack Vector Mitigation Matrix
Create `ops/security/THREAT_MODEL.md`:

| Vector | Current Defense | Gap | Ops Enhancement |
|---|---|---|---|
| CSRF | Double-submit cookie | WS bypass audit needed | `csrf-coverage-audit.ts` |
| XSS | React escaping, Helmet (if present) | Verify CSP headers | `ops/alerts/csp-violation-alert.yaml` |
| CSV Injection | `csvEscape` in export workers | Verify `=+-@` prefix nullification | `csv-injection-fuzzer.ts` |
| SSRF | N/A | MinIO internal endpoints reachable | NetworkPolicy already blocks external |
| Data Exfiltration | Signed URL TTL, admin auth | Volume-based alerting missing | `SuspiciousExportVolume` alert |
| DDoS | Ingress RPS 200, connections 100 | No per-endpoint granularity | `ops/alerts/ddos-escalation.yaml` |
| Brute Force | Login rate limit (IP+email) | Admin panel rate limit gaps | Verify [adminDataExports.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminDataExports.ts) limiter |
| Replay | Session tokens with expiry | WS message replay risk | Session trail in [sessionTrail.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/security/sessionTrail.ts) |

### A5. CSV Injection Fuzzer
- **File:** `ops/security/csv-injection-fuzzer.ts`
- **Logic:** Insert test users with names `=cmd|'/C calc'!A0`, `+1+1`, `-1+1`, `@SUM(A1)`. Trigger export via [adminDataExportBuild.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/adminDataExportBuild.ts). Download artifact from MinIO. Assert no cell starts with `=`, `+`, `-`, `@` without a leading `'` escape.

