## WS-E: Chaos Engineering & Pre-Flight Validation

### E1. `ops/chaos/billion-row-synthetic.ts`
- Generate 1,000,000 synthetic trade rows with realistic schema matching [shared/schema.pg.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/schema.pg.ts) `trades` table.
- Bulk insert into ClickHouse via [clickhouseClient.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/clickhouseClient.ts) connection.
- Query `kpi-summary` equivalent aggregation and assert < 1s response.

### E2. `ops/chaos/valkey-eviction-stress.js`
- Flood Valkey with 500MB of generic keys.
- Verify `redis_evicted_keys_total` increments and BullMQ queues remain functional.
- Assert no export jobs are lost during eviction pressure.

### E3. `ops/chaos/queue-crash-recovery.sh`
- Enqueue 1,000 export jobs via API.
- `kubectl delete pod -l role=worker --force` mid-processing.
- Wait for pod recreation.
- Assert all jobs eventually complete (no orphans).

### E4. `ops/chaos/pgbouncer-connection-storm.js`
- Open 10,000 concurrent TCP connections to PgBouncer.
- Assert PgBouncer rejects gracefully (no Postgres crash, no OOM).

### E5. `ops/chaos/tls-downgrade-test.sh`
- Attempt to connect to the ingress on port 80 (HTTP).
- Assert 301/308 redirect to HTTPS.
- Attempt TLS 1.0/1.1 connection. Assert rejection.

