## WS-F: Incident Response Runbooks

### F1. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_EXPORT_PIPELINE_STALL.md`
- Trigger: `ExportQueueStarvation` or `ExportThroughputStalled`
- Steps: Check worker pod status via Headlamp → `kubectl logs -n tradehub -l role=worker --tail=100` → Check Valkey connectivity → Check MinIO bucket write permissions → Manually advance stalled jobs via [adminDataExportQueue.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/adminDataExportQueue.ts) recovery functions.

### F2. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_ANALYTICS_STALENESS.md`
- Trigger: `RollupRefreshStale` or `ClickHouseSyncLagCritical`
- Steps: Check [clickhouseSync.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/clickhouseSync.ts) high-watermark state → Verify Postgres→CH network path → Manual sync trigger → Full rollup rebuild command.

### F3. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_DDOS_DOS_RESPONSE.md`
- Trigger: Ingress RPS spike, `BruteForceLoginAttempts`
- Steps: Check OVH Anti-DDoS dashboard → Tighten [30-ingress.yaml](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/k8s/30-ingress.yaml) `limit-rps` → IP blocklist via ConfigMap → Escalate to OVH support if volumetric.

### F4. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_DATA_EXFILTRATION.md`
- Trigger: `SuspiciousExportVolume`
- Steps: Identify admin account from export job audit trail → Freeze account via [adminScopeSession.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/security/adminScopeSession.ts) → Invalidate all active Pre-Signed URLs (MinIO bucket policy update) → Preserve forensic logs.

### F5. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_CACHE_COLLAPSE.md`
- Trigger: `ValkeyMemoryPressure` or `CacheHitRateDegraded`
- Steps: Check `redis_used_memory_bytes` → Flush non-critical keys → Verify `maxmemory-policy` is `allkeys-lru` → Scale Valkey memory limit in [k8s/05-valkey.yaml](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/k8s/05-valkey.yaml).

### F6. `ops/runbooks/RUNBOOK_INTERNAL_TLS.md`
- Reference document for enabling TLS on internal services (Valkey, ClickHouse, MinIO) when moving from dev to production topology.

